  "query_preview": "..With clear skies in place across the region, patchy\nfog is expected to develop in fog prone areas such as the Cache \nValley. Fog will dissipate through Sunday morning, with additional\nchances for fog development overnight Sunday decreasing due to\nincreasing cloud cover across northern Utah. \n\nQuiescent conditions with a gradual warming trend prevails into\nearly this upcoming week as longwave ridging remains the dominant\nfeature across the region. Warming aloft through this period will\nallow valley inversions to strengthen, resulting in hazy skies. A\nweak shortwave trough is slated to traverse northern Utah on\nTuesday, ushering in slightly cooler air aloft, which may assist\nin mixing out some valley haze. Following the departure of this\nweak wave, high pressure re-amplifies across the region in\nresponse to a trough deepening off the west coast. \n\nEnsembles have diverged in the progression of the aforementioned\ntrough as we head into next weekend, with around 20% of members\nsupportive of a shortwave ejecting off the parent trough and\nbringing increased chances for precipitation as early as Saturday.\nThe remainder of models eject this energy too far south for any\nmeaningful precipitation outside of slight chances across southern\nUtah. Regardless, the pattern looks to remain more progressive,\nthough the exact storm track is uncertain at this point.",
